[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m[Lyn Alden](https://www.lynalden.com/)[0m                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mInvestment Strategy[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m7 Top Stocks to Buy and Hold for the Next Decade and Beyond[0m                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m===========================================================[0m                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![7 Top Stocks to Buy and Hold for the Next Decade and Beyond](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-to-buy-feature.jpg)[0m                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHundreds of thousands of people search for terms like “stocks to buy today” or “best stocks to buy” or “top stocks for 2024” every single month.[0m             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe appeal is understandable, but most of the articles that pop up are ones quickly written by freelancers that often don’t even invest in the stocks they [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpitch. They’re just writing for one-time clicks and pageviews rather than doing serious research to provide value and establish long-term relationships [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwith their readers.[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe truth is, investing is hard, and building a portfolio of top stocks to buy that beat the market is something that even financial professionals have [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mtrouble doing consistently.[0m                                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn fact, after fees, only about 11% of actively-managed funds outperform the S&P 500 over a significant period of time:[0m                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks Fund Outperformance](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-fund-outperformance.png)[0m                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m*Chart Source: [S&P 500 SPIVA](https://us.spindices.com/spiva/#/reports)*[0m                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFor the average non-professional investor, it’s even worse. As calculated by Dalbar Inc, and charted here by JP Morgan, the average investor underperforms [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32ma 60/40 equity/bond portfolio:[0m                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks Average Investor](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-average-investor.png)[0m                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m*Chart Source: [JP Morgan Guide to the Markets](https://am.jpmorgan.com/us/en/asset-management/gim/adv/insights/guide-to-the-markets)*[0m                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThat’s mainly because investors tend to buy stocks or funds during market tops when they are expensive and all the news is good, and then sell stocks and [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfunds *after* they crash, when they are cheap. They keep doing that over years and the returns end up being below a buy-and-hold baseline.[0m                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMeanwhile, value investors like Warren Buffett are building up cash during euphoric bull markets, because everything is expensive and very few stocks meet [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mtheir strict investment criteria. Then when a [stock market crash](https://www.lynalden.com/stock-market-crash-bear-market/) eventually occurs and top [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mstocks are on sale everywhere, they deploy their cash hoard and snatch up the bargains of a decade.[0m                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHowever, there are plenty of independent, disciplined investors that [build serious wealth](https://www.lynalden.com/build-wealth/) in the market over the [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlong term by following similar methods. It’s simple, but not easy, to stay focused and buy high-quality companies at reasonable prices on a consistent [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbasis.[0m                                                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mInvestment Criteria for Top Stocks[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m----------------------------------[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEven though markets are hard to outperform, I think individual stocks can be a valuable component of an investor’s portfolio.[0m                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAs I explained in [my article about investor psychology](https://www.lynalden.com/beat-the-market/), the most important thing you can do is find the right [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32minvestment strategy for your unique needs and personality. You need a strategy that performs well, but also one that you’re comfortable with and that will [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mentice you to invest regularly.[0m                                                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFor many people, that’s index funds. In fact, I think most people should hold some index funds.[0m                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBut I think [dividend growth investing](https://www.lynalden.com/blue-chip-dividend-stocks/) is a good strategy for many hands-on people as well. This [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmeans investing in companies with 10+ years of consecutive dividend growth, sustainable dividend payout ratios, and solid growth prospects.[0m                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAs a strategy, it provides more reliable investment income than index funds, gives investors an opportunity to learn about a variety of businesses, and [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mturns on the “collector’s instinct” in a lot of people that can get them excited to invest more money.[0m                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhile index funds can seem distant and vague, buying and holding a collection of hand-picked dividend stocks that grow their dividends every year at an [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mexponential pace just “clicks” for a lot of people, and builds good investing habits. Some people like to know what they own. Dividend growth stocks as a [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mgroup have statistically mildly outperformed the S&P 500 for decades too, which doesn’t hurt.[0m                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mYou can buy shares of companies, those shares produce cash dividends that grow each year, and you can reinvest those dividends into more shares or you can [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mspend them.[0m                                                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mRather than just hoping the stock price moves up rather than down, dividend investors tend to pay attention to the underlying fundamentals of the company, [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mincluding the growth and safety of their dividends, and watch for strong long-term performance. This helps build good investment fundamentals because they [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfocus on company performance more-so than fluctuations in the daily stock price.[0m                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWith that said, here are the 8 main criteria I used when selecting top stocks to highlight for this article:[0m                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 1:** The company benefits from long-term trends and has little foreseeable risk of obsolescence.[0m                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 2:** The company has above-average returns on invested capital and a durable economic moat to keep it that way.[0m                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 3:** The company has a strong balance sheet, and solid historical performance during recessions.[0m                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 4:**The company is a premium provider. They compete over quality, rather than just on price.[0m                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 5:**The company generally has management with long tenures and a focus on long-term results.[0m                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 6:**The company enjoys profitable growth. Not growth at all costs, but a combination of sustainable growth and value.[0m                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 7:**The company is trading for a reasonable valuation. It’s a fair price for an exceptional company.[0m                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Criteria 8:**The company is in my personal portfolio. I’ve researched and followed it for years, and understand its various nuances.[0m                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mI didn’t directly include a dividend metric for this article, because I already have two popular dividend articles that I keep fresh with stock ideas:[0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* [5 Rock-Solid Blue Chip Dividend Stocks I’m Bullish On](https://www.lynalden.com/blue-chip-dividend-stocks/)[0m                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* [Safe High Dividend Stocks: 15+ Strong Picks](https://www.lynalden.com/safe-high-dividend-stocks/)[0m                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mTherefore, some of the companies in this article have rather low dividend yields or in some rare cases no dividends, and that’s okay. The focus here is on [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mtotal risk-adjusted returns.[0m                                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFor many of the stocks on the list below, I use F.A.S.T. Graphs to illustrate their stock price relative to their fundamentals. On these graphs, the black [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mline represents the share price, the blue line represents what the share price would be if it were trading at its average 20-year multiple of earnings [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m(i.e. its average valuation), and the white line represents dividends per share that year.[0m                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhen it comes to investing, nothing is for certain. There are no perfect stocks to buy, because there’s no way to see the future perfectly.[0m                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHowever, buying a diversified portfolio of high-quality companies at reasonable prices is among the most reliable ways to build wealth over the long-term.[0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m7 Great Stocks To Buy and Hold[0m                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m------------------------------[0m                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHere are seven companies that I think are trading at reasonable valuations that offer strong risk-adjusted returns over the next decade, and meet the [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mabove-mentioned criteria.[0m                                                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAll of these are companies I actually own for the long-term. They’re ones I’ve researched for years, and some of which I have quite large positions in.[0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSome of these are likely to beat the market over time, while some may not. They have all beaten the market in the past. In terms of risk-adjusted returns, [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthese are among the stocks I’m most comfortable holding through all market conditions along with my index funds. Always do your own due diligence before [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbuying any company.[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mI published the first version of this article in 2018, and all 7 stocks that were selected outperformed the S&P 500 over the subsequent year. I then [0m        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mupdated this article in subsequent years, and as of this writing have updated it at the start of 2024.[0m                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #1) Enterprise Products Partners (EPD)[0m                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Enterprise Partners Best Stock](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/enterprise-best-stock-updated.png)[0m                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise Products Partners LP (EPD) is one of the largest midstream companies in North America.[0m                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThey operate a vast pipeline network that transports oil, gas, refined products, and petrochemicals. They play a key role in the growing US liquified [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mnatural gas market,[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAlthough not without occasional incidents, pipelines are safer and more cost-effective for transporting various liquids and gases than their main [0m           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32malternative, which is by freight train.[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise has little direct exposure to commodity prices; they make money mainly by transporting energy, refined products, and petrochemicals. However, [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mprolonged periods of low energy prices can reduce production volumes, which eventually means lower volumes and lower revenue for transporters like [0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise.[0m                                                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOne of the things I like best about Enterprise is how diversified they are. Rather than being merely an oil and gas play, their exposure to refined [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mproducts and petrochemicals gives them strong future-proof growth, and resilience against changes in market conditions.[0m                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks: EPD Product Mix](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stocks-epd-product-mix.png)[0m                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise currently has a distribution yield of over 7.5% and 25 years of consecutive annual distribution growth:[0m                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks: Enterprise Products Partners FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-enterprise-fastgraphs.png)[0m                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWith a high dividend yield, a dividend payout ratio that is well-supported by distributable cash flows, and solid dividend growth expected going forward, [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise offers a high likelihood of strong total returns for the next decade.[0m                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**EPD Economic Moat Rating: 5 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mPipelines and related energy infrastructure has a rather wide economic moat. Once a pipeline is built to supply a certain area, it’s generally uneconomic [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfor a competitor to build a similar pipeline. New pipelines generally are built when the needs of a region are structurally undersupplied, and at that [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpoint, it’s often economic for the same company to expand their existing volume on the same footprint with a secondary pipeline, rather than for a [0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcompetitor to copy it.[0m                                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mPolitical opposition can prevent the construction of certain pipelines. This slows down growth of some northern pipeline companies, but also ironically [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mincreases the importance of existing pipeline infrastructure.[0m                                                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**EPD Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEnterprise has constantly maintained one of the highest credit ratings and lowest debt ratios in the midstream industry, which is what allowed them to keep[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mraising their distribution over the years rather than having to cut it during downturns. In other words, they invested like the tortoise, not the hare. [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mTheir balance sheet is rated A-, and there is no midstream operator with a higher rating.[0m                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mStill, any asset-heavy business like this currently uses a lot of leverage. They have a long bond maturity profile and rather low interest rates on debt [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthat is mostly fixed-rate.[0m                                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #2) Brookfield Corporation (BN)[0m                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks: Brookfield Asset Management](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stock-bam.jpg)[0m                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBrookfield Corporation (BN) is a Canadian financial firm you might or might not have heard of. It’s an asset manager that specializes in real assets like [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mproperty, infrastructure, and renewable energy.[0m                                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mTheir roots trace back over a century, when the company was an early developer and operator of infrastructure in Brazil. Currently they have over 200,000 [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32memployees.[0m                                                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOver the past 20 years, they have expanded into a global asset manager with over $850 billion in assets under management. They have diverse properties [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mincluding gas pipelines, toll roads, data centers, solar farms, hydroelectric dams, and skyscrapers across five continents.[0m                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThey hold the controlling stake in five publicly traded entities:[0m                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Brookfield Asset Management (BAM)[0m                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Brookfield Renewable Partners (BEP)[0m                                                                                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Brookfield Infrastructure Partners (BIP)[0m                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Brookfield Business Partners (BBU)[0m                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Brookfield Reinsurance (BNRE)[0m                                                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAs a private equity firm, they make money in three main ways. First, they invest their own capital into a variety of real assets. Second, they collect [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmoney from institutional investors, invest that money on behalf of them into a variety of real assets, and collect management and performance fees from [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthat capital. Third, they founded and hold large stakes in the above-mentioned publicly traded partnerships, from which they collect cash distributions, [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmanagement fees, and performance fees.[0m                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThis structure gives them strong growth, because in addition to their direct investments being extremely profitable, they are also benefiting from a major [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mtrend of increased institutional allocations into alternative assets, like private equity, real estate, infrastructure, credit, and other high-performing [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlow-liquidity investments. Brookfield’s private funds have consistently beaten benchmarks like the S&P 500.[0m                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mInsiders own a large portion of the company, worth billions of dollars. So, their incentives are highly aligned with shareholders. The CEO, Bruce Flatt, [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mhas been with the company for over three decades, has been CEO for over half that time, and has overseen tremendous performance during his tenure so far.[0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mDespite Brookfield’s astounding long-term results, they are not well-known and in my opinion they are still reasonably priced. Since they own [0m               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcash-producing stakes in multiple partnerships and have a complex corporate structure, BN tends not to show up well on stock screeners, and people looking [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mat their financial statements for the first time wouldn’t see anything that stands out. In fact, they always look overvalued at first glance because their [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mreported earnings tend to be choppy.[0m                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn addition, they have a sizable allocation to commercial property, and commercial property is *struggling* right now due to higher interest rates and [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwork-from-home trends.[0m                                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSo, they tend to fly under the radar compared to a lot of top stocks that are household names.[0m                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe company positions itself well for recessions, because management builds up a fortress balance sheet, and then buys great assets for bargain prices from[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mdistressed sellers.[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOften, companies take on too much debt, their credit ratings drop, their interest yields get too high, and then when something unexpected hurts them, they [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mgo bankrupt or need to sell assets at fire-sale prices. Brookfield buys them, refinances them to much lower interest rates thanks to their high credit [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mrating, and makes strong returns as they hold and expand those assets. Often, they sell those assets during bull markets for much higher valuation [0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmultiples than they paid, so that they can recycle that capital back into other distressed assets.[0m                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFor example, during the 2007/2008 financial crisis, Brookfield bought a variety of undervalued shipping ports, rail infrastructure, and other global assets[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfrom a firm called Babcock & Brown that ran into too much debt and got liquidated. These assets performed tremendously as the global economy recovered.[0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBack when Chile was a frontier market without much investor interest, Brookfield bought cheap electrical transmission assets, expanded them for over a [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mdecade, and sold them over a decade later for a 16% annually compounded return.[0m                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhen Brazil ran into a huge recession during 2014-2017, Brookfield acquired all sorts of gas pipelines and toll roads from distressed sellers that needed [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mto raise capital, and locked in long-term favorable pricing contracts indexed to inflation.[0m                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhen North American midstream companies ran into major trouble in 2015-2018 due to energy oversupply and low prices, Brookfield bought energy [0m               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mtransportation infrastructure on the cheap.[0m                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAfter solar developer SunEdison collapsed into bankruptcy from too much debt to fuel overly-aggressive growth plans, Brookfield swooped in and bought lots [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mof attractively-priced solar and wind farms from them.[0m                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn early 2018 when the retail sector was under intense pressure from the existential threat of online retail, Brookfield bought out General Growth [0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mProperties, which has a lot of best-in-class properties and high occupancy rates. Some of this they will retain as retail, while other assets they will [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mredevelop into other types of property.[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn 2020, BN’s office towers were pressured by COVID-19, but their renewable energy and infrastructure businesses performed very well, and they have been [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcontinuing to add bolt-on acquisitions to their various platforms.[0m                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe point is, Brookfield management consists of [contrarian investors](https://www.lynalden.com/contrarian-investing/). They buy undervalued (but premium [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mquality) assets during times of stress, expand them, and sell them for much higher valuations during bull markets.[0m                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAlthough Brookfield Corporation pays a low dividend yield, most of the returns come from capital appreciation over time. Their various partnerships, on the[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mother hand, offer higher yields with a bit less growth.[0m                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks: Brookfield FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stocks-brookfield-fastgraph.png)[0m                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**BN Economic Moat Rating: 5 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBrookfield Corporation (BN) has a globally diversified portfolio of real assets, including utilities, utility-like regulated monopoly infrastructure, [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpremium buildings in world-class cities like London and Manhattan, and a large collection of hydroelectric dams. These are among the types of assets with [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthe widest available economic moats. Being so globally diversified also reduces their reliance on any one nation’s economy or politics.[0m                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn addition, asset managers benefit from high switching costs, and Brookfield Asset Management (BAM) in particular does. Private equity funds typically [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlock in investors for many years. And as long as BAM private funds continue to perform well, institutional investors should continue to reinvest in them [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwhen they have the opportunity to do so. BN is the majority shareholder in BAM.[0m                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**BN Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBrookfield Corporation (BN) has plenty of liquidity, and much of its debt is non-recourse to the parent corporation, but due to its complex corporate [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mstructure with multiple layers of moderate leverage, it has a moderate investment-grade credit rating from most rating agencies. S&P for example assigns it[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32man A-.[0m                                                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #3) MicroStrategy (MSTR)[0m                                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![MicroStrategy Overview](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-microstrategy.png)[0m                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy (MSTR) is a business analytics and intelligence company founded in 1989 that has outlived many of its peers throughout the past three and a [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mhalf decades. They’re perhaps most well known for holding bitcoin on their balance sheet, which has been their differentiated strategy since August 2020 [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwhen bitcoin was worth around $10,000.[0m                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAnd since adoption of that strategy, they have outperformed all major stock indices and even bitcoin itself.[0m                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![MicroStrategy Returns](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/microstrategy-returns.png)[0m                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOver time, a lot of the tech monopoly companies have eaten their smaller competition. It’s hard to survive as a small or medium-sized tech company for a [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlong time. As a result, most business analytics companies have been acquired into larger entities or have gone out of business, with MicroStrategy being [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mone of the sole survivors as a separate company.[0m                                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy had structurally rising revenue until 2014. After that, their revenue started to diminish for a while, and then began stabilizing and going [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32msideways. The company held very large cash reserves and no debt, but the market didn’t reward them for that fortress balance sheet, and their cash reserves[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32munderperformed other types of assets. In response to the pandemic/lockdown stimulus of 2020, where money supply grew massively, the company’s then-CEO and [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcurrent executive chairman, Michael Saylor, worked with the board to pivot their reserves practices to avoid having their reserves be heavily debased. They[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mdecided to put their cash reserves into bitcoin instead, which has strong network effects and a finite supply.[0m                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Bitcoin Supply](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/21-B.png)[0m                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMany companies return value to shareholders through dividends and share repurchases. That’s better than holding large amounts of debasing cash, and much [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbetter than doing non-strategic acquisitions. MicroStrategy also wants to avoid non-strategic acquisitions, but instead of decapitalizing their company, [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthey put their retained earnings into bitcoin and build up a huge company treasury. They’re now tapped into a large and growing network effect, and thus [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mhave some bulwark to compete with the tech titans. As long as the Bitcoin network remains robust and its overall value and liquidity improve over time, [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy should have tailwinds behind it.[0m                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy will be the most controversial pick on this list by far. If you expect bitcoin to outperform the S&P 500 for the next 5-10 years (as it has [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mover the past 5-10 years), then MicroStrategy will likely outperform as well. On the other hand, if you expect bitcoin to fail or stagnate, then [0m            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy will run into similarly bad headwinds. Definitely do not purchase MicroStrategy if you are not long-term bullish on the price of bitcoin.[0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIf you’re not sure either way, and want to learn more about the past, present, and future through the lens of technology, then my book [*Broken [0m             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMoney*](https://www.amazon.com/Broken-Money-Financial-System-Failing/dp/B0CG8985FR) is a recommended read.[0m                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Bitcoin vs Top Stocks](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/bitcoin-vs-top-stocks.png)[0m                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**MSTR Economic Moat Rating: 3 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy provides differentiated services, including subscription cloud services with high retention rates. However, as a smallish tech company, [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthey’re competing with titans, and that has been their long-term challenge. That’s part of the reason they began using their balance sheet more actively [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mrather than just their income statement.[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**MSTR Balance Sheet Rating: 5? out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMicroStrategy has the hardest balance sheet to rate objectively, because ultimately it comes down to whether bitcoin will continue to be successful. An [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32minvestor that is bullish on bitcoin will look at MicroStrategy’s balance sheet and see a fortress, and is the key thing that will allow them to keep up [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwith bigger competition. Meanwhile, an investor that is bearish on bitcoin will look at MicroStrategy’s balance sheet and see a disaster in the making.[0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #4) HDFC Bank (HDB)[0m                                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![HDFC Bank Top Stock](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stock-hdfc-bank.png)[0m                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHDFC Bank is the largest private bank in India, having been founded in 1994, and it now has thousands of branches and a robust online business throughout [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIndia.[0m                                                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks: HDB FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-hdb-fastgraph.png)[0m                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIndia is set to overtake China as the world’s most populous country, and still has very low (but rising) per-capita GDP. As a large emerging market, it has[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mone of the highest GDP growth rates in the world, and is set to become one of the world’s largest economies by the 2030s.[0m                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHDFC stock is available as an ADR on the NYSE under the ticker HDB. You can see below, with data since its inception on the public markets, how fast its [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mearnings are growing relative to a large U.S. bank like J.P. Morgan Chase:[0m                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks HDFC vs JDP Earnings Growth](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stocks-hdb-vs-jpm-earnings.png)[0m                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m*Chart Source: Y Charts*[0m                                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBesides all of the normal risks that come from operating a bank, HDFC Bank’s stock has two key risks.[0m                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFirst of all, it is not cheap, with a blended P/E ratio of over 22 at the moment. However, with earnings growing at over 15% per year, it actually has a [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mrather attractive [PEG ratio](https://www.lynalden.com/pe-ratio/), which was a metric popularized by Peter Lynch that compares the valuation of a company [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mto its growth rate.[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSecond, India is very reliant on oil imports, and whenever oil becomes expensive, their trade deficit widens, which tends to hurt the currency. If you’re [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32man American or European investor, for example, then you don’t really care how HDFC Bank stock performs in terms of Indian rupees; you care how it performs [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32min dollars and euros. If the rupee weakens vs those currencies, your returns could be reduced. On the other hand, if the rupee strengthens vs your home [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcurrency, it’s a tailwind.[0m                                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mPersonally, I think having a stake in India as part of a diversified portfolio, and letting it run for the next decade, is a smart thing to do. I like the [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mINDA ETF, but I also like HDFC Bank stock, particularly.[0m                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**HDB Economic Moat Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHDFC Bank has built up significant economy of scale within India, which gives it operational advantages over competitors. In addition, banks tend to have [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mannoying switching costs, meaning that once customers pick a bank, they don’t change too frequently.[0m                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**HDB Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHDFC Bank maintains strong creditworthiness, but as a bank in a developing country, it can be subject to more severe currency fluctuations or other crises [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcompared to what is historically normal for developed markets.[0m                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #5) Canadian Natural Resources (CNQ)[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![The Case for a Longer-Term Oil and Gas Bull Market](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/oil-and-gas-feature-image.jpg)[0m                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe world tends to undergo cycles of major investment between financial assets and real assets.[0m                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mDuring periods of scarcity for things like commodities and infrastructure, inflation runs hot, and the world begins building mines and various [0m              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32minfrastructure projects, up until it leads to a period of oversupply.[0m                                                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThat oversupplied environment leads to disinflation and lower interest rates, which is good for promoting higher asset prices. Investors can buy income [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mstreams and lever them up with cheap debt, and can use equity as compensation for unprofitable high-growth companies. Eventually, this environment runs its[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcourse, as asset prices become excessive, and the period of real-world oversupply ends.[0m                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe 1940s were about real assets, while the 1950s and 1960s were more about financialization. The 1970s were once again about real assets, while the 1980s [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mand 1990s were more about financialization. The 2000s were once again about real assets, while the 2010s and early 2020s were more about financialization. [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIf the world collectively enters another period of emphasizing real assets, then energy producers are a key industry to have exposure to.[0m                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mUS shale oil producers tend to have rapid decline rates. In other words, they drill a well, and within a few years that well is mostly dry. They have to [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mkeep drilling more and more wells just to maintain current production, let alone grow it.[0m                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOn the other hand, deep water wells and oil sands tend to have the opposite dynamic. Their upfront development costs are much higher, but from there the [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mhave a very long period of production with a low decline rate.[0m                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCanadian Natural Resources focuses primarily on the latter, especially with their oil sands. The company has very long-life reserves and major free cash [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mflow generation potential due to a lot of upfront capital expenditures already having been performed.[0m                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Top Stocks: CNQ FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/top-stocks-cnq-fastgraph.png)[0m                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Canadian Natural Resources Economic Moat Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCanadian Natural Resources’ moat is limited by the fact that just like any commodity producer, it can’t control the price of its products (oil and gas).[0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThat being said, the have among the longest reserves relative to their annual production rate, and therefore have a long runway of profits ahead.[0m            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Canadian Natural Resources Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWith a BBB- credit rating, Canadian Natural Resources probably has the weakest balance sheet on this list, officially.[0m                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mHowever, it’s headed in the right direction. They significantly reduced their net debt over the past couple years, to the point where one year’s worth of [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mnet income is higher than their total net debt. Whether income can remain this high will largely depend on energy prices, but the company has taken the [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mprudent action of funneling large percentages of their incoming cash flows towards strengthening the balance sheet.[0m                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #6) CVS Health (CVS)[0m                                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks: CVS Health](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-cvs-logo.png)[0m                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCVS Health (CVS) is one of the largest companies in the world ranked by revenue. They operate a large retail pharmacy chain, a health insurance provider, [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mand a pharmacy benefits manager.[0m                                                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe stock became rather overvalued in 2014 and has since declined quite a bit, while their earnings per share kept increasing. In recent years, the company[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mperformed a handful of transformative acquisitions to position themselves as a leading multi-vertical healthcare provider.[0m                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks: CVS FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-cvs-fastgraph-1.png)[0m                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**CVS Economic Moat Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAs a vertically-integrated healthcare company, combining a retail pharmacy chain, health insurance provider, and pharmacy benefits manager, CVS has [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcemented itself pretty well into the US healthcare landscape. They do face an issue of rather low switching costs between pharmacies, but their other [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbusinesses create longer-term relationships with clients.[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**CVS Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCVS has a BBB credit rating, which is rather average. However, their balance sheet strength is sharply moving in the right direction, ever since their [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAetna acquisition. In addition, they are more diversified across business lines than they used to be.[0m                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### #7) Intercontinental Exchange (ICE)[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks: Intercontinental Exchange](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-intercontinental-exchange.jpg)[0m                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIntercontinental Exchange (ICE) owns a number of exchanges and clearing houses around the world, with the New York Stock Exchange being the most venerable [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mamong them.[0m                                                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThat’s right, you can buy shares of the New York Stock Exchange… on the New York Stock Exchange. However, they also handle major trading volume for [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcommodity futures and over-the-counter markets.[0m                                                                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhat makes an exchange attractive is that they have relatively fixed costs, while their revenues are quite variable and can grow in line with inflation and[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpopulation. Especially after the recent sharp correction in ICE’s share price, I think it’s pretty interesting going into 2024.[0m                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![Best Stocks: ICE FAST Graph](https://www.lynalden.com/wp-content/uploads/best-stocks-ice-fastgraph-1.png)[0m                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**ICE Economic Moat Rating: 5 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSecurities exchanges historically have enjoyed about the strongest economic moats that any company can have. Once one develops, that is where the trading [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mliquidity is, and smaller exchanges are rather irrelevant in comparison because they lack liquidity. Liquidity then tends to consolidate towards the [0m        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbiggest, as a strong network effect. This is then further supported by regulatory guardrails.[0m                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe digital tokenization of existing securities represents a potential change in the type of tech rails that trading and settlement happens on, so ICE and [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mothers will need to be vigilant about modernizing their backend systems. Technology switchovers represent periods of time where existing moats can be lost,[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mso that is a risk worth monitoring.[0m                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**ICE Balance Sheet Rating: 4 out of 5**[0m                                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mICE has been a rather aggressive grower and acquirer, at times taking on significant debt to do so. A series of bad investments could derail the financial [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mplans of the company. Overall, the company has a strong A- credit rating, and maintains a very reasonable ratio of net debt to annual free cash flow.[0m        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAsset Allocation vs Hot Stock Selection[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m---------------------------------------[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m[Asset allocation](https://www.lynalden.com/asset-allocation/), meaning the long-term strategy for how you invest in various asset classes, is more [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mimportant for most investors than individual stock selection.[0m                                                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFocusing all your time on trying to pick the top stocks usually results in missing the forest by looking for the trees.[0m                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mGetting the big questions right, like how much of your net worth should be in domestic equities, how much you should invest in [international [0m               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mstocks](https://www.lynalden.com/international-stocks/), how much to invest in bonds or precious metals, how reliably you [re-balance your [0m                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mportfolio](https://www.lynalden.com/how-to-invest-money/), and how consistently you [save money](https://www.lynalden.com/save-money/) to invest, are [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlikely to generate the bulk of your returns and portfolio growth compared to spending a lot of time looking for the top stocks to buy.[0m                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mEveryone has that colleague at work that talks about how their portfolio did this quarter, or about some hot stock they recently bought. You know the type [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mof guy. Ten years later he’s still talking about trading a couple thousand bucks in stocks around but is he rich yet?[0m                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIt doesn’t matter what stocks you pick if you don’t a) diligently put capital to work month after month with a high savings rate and b) focus on long-term [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mresults and building wealth.[0m                                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThere are some highly-skilled traders out there that make a lot of money in the short term by devoting their full-time job to it, but most of the people [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwho get rich from the stock market are people with day jobs that diligently save and invest money every paycheck.[0m                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThey keep buying and holding dividend stocks, index funds, real estate, or other high quality assets with a focus on long-term results.[0m                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAnd as I said before, I’m in favor of buying individual stocks, at least for some people. I think it’s a valuable practice to be able to understand and [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mvalue a business, and evidence shows that some value-oriented strategies with a long-term focus do indeed outperform the broader market.[0m                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mBut it’s important not to get obsessed with it, or concentrate too heavily in any individual hot stock.[0m                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFinal Thoughts[0m                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m--------------[0m                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
