[32m│[0m  [32mWhat Makes a ‘Best Company’?[0m                                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m----------------------------[0m                                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOne of the keys to finding the best long-term investments is buying good companies that can stay one step ahead of the competition. [Legendary investor [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWarren Buffett](https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/how-invest-like-warren-buffett) originally coined the term “[economic [0m                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmoat](https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/how-measure-companys-competitive-advantage)” to refer to a company’s ability to keep competitors at bay over time.[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMorningstar builds on this idea to rate companies based on their “moat,” or the strength and durability of their competitive edge.[0m                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe have compiled a list of the best companies to invest in under our analysts’ coverage that are available to US investors. These companies have [0m            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32msuccessfully carved out wide moats between them and their industry competitors, and we’re confident that they will produce returns that outweigh their [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcosts for the next 20 years or more. In other words, these are good companies that will reliably be able to produce returns for investors over a long [0m       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mperiod, even as they invest in their growth.[0m                                                                                                                 [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mA company’s longevity and competitive advantage are inherently tied to sustainability, so [our analysis takes environmental, social, and governance [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mconsiderations](https://www.morningstar.com/sustainable-investing/incorporating-esg-into-our-equity-research-process) into account. The best companies have[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbusiness models that allow them to effectively navigate evolving ESG issues that could materially affect their business. Cutting corners or taking on too [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmuch risk may work in the short run, but these tactics won’t give a company enduring success.[0m                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe companies that make our list also have predictable cash flows (or predictable amounts of money going into and out of a company), so our analysts can [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmore accurately estimate how much the businesses are worth. These companies also make smart decisions about how they manage and invest their money.[0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe aren’t advocating that you buy shares of every company on this list today. Even the greatest company can be a bad investment [if you [0m                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32moverpay](https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/how-determine-whether-stock-is-cheap-expensive-or-fairly-valued). The share prices of many companies on this [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlist overestimate their real value, so it may not be the right time to buy. Still, we believe these companies are essential for any stock investor’s [0m        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mwatchlist. Check out “[The 10 Best Companies to Invest in Now](https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/10-best-companies-invest-now)” to find the most [0m           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mundervalued companies on our list.[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
