[32m│[0m  [32mBest Companies to Own: Methodology[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m----------------------------------[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThe companies on this list are covered by Morningstar Research Services’ equity analysts and have shares available to US investors. This means that [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mMorningstar equity analysts have calculated[0m                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfair value estimates[0m                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mfor the shares of the companies that trade on US exchanges. As a result, most of the companies on this list are based in the US.[0m                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWithin that coverage list, the best companies meet the following criteria:[0m                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Wide Economic Moat.** The[0m                                                                                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  Morningstar Economic Moat Rating[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  summarizes the length of a company’s competitive advantages. An economic moat is a structural feature allowing a firm to generate excess profits over a [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlong period. If Morningstar Research Services believes that excess returns will persist for 20 years or more, that company earns a wide moat rating.[0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Standard or Exemplary Capital Allocation.** The stock’s[0m                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  Morningstar Capital Allocation Rating[0m                                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  is an assessment of the quality of management’s capital allocation, with particular emphasis on the firm’s balance sheet, investments, and shareholder [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mdistributions. Capital allocation is judged from an equity shareholder’s perspective, considering companies’ investment strategy and valuation, [0m             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbalance-sheet management, and dividend and share buyback policies on a forward-looking basis. A company can receive an Exemplary, Standard, or Poor Capital[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAllocation Rating.[0m                                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Low or Medium Fair Value Uncertainty.** The fair value[0m                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  Morningstar Uncertainty Rating[0m                                                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m  represents the predictability of a company’s future cash flows and, therefore, the level of certainty in the fair value estimate of that company. The [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mUncertainty Rating for a company can be Low, Medium, High, Very High, or Extreme. It captures a range of likely potential intrinsic values for a company [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbased on the characteristics of the business underlying the stock, including such things as operating and financial leverage, sales sensitivity to the [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32meconomy, product concentration, and other factors. The more predictable the cash flows, the smaller the range of potential intrinsic values, and the lower [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthe uncertainty.[0m                                                                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWhat Gives a Company an Economic Moat?[0m                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m--------------------------------------[0m                                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCompanies with moats have one or more of the following characteristics:[0m                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Network Effect.** Lots of people are using the service, which then makes the service more valuable to the people who use it.[0m                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Intangible Assets.** Patents, brands, regulatory licenses, and other intangible assets can prevent competitors from duplicating a company’s products or[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mallow the company to charge a significant price premium.[0m                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Cost Advantage.** Firms with a structural cost advantage can either undercut competitors on price while earning similar margins or charge market-level [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mprices while earning relatively high margins.[0m                                                                                                                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Switching Costs.** When it would be too expensive or troublesome to stop using a company’s products, the company often has pricing power.[0m                [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* **Efficient Scale.** When a niche market is effectively served by one or a small handful of companies, there is no room or incentive for potential [0m        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcompetitors to enter the market.[0m                                                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mTo maintain analysts’ independence, Morningstar Research Services does not publicly rate its parent company, Morningstar. Therefore, Morningstar is not on [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthe list of the best companies available to US investors.[0m                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
