[32m│[0m  [32mQuality stocks for uncertain times[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m==================================[0m                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn a shifting world, consider best-in-class companies.[0m                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFidelity Viewpoints[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m![](/bin-public/600_Fidelity_Com_English/images/learning-center/heros/quality-stocks-for-uncertain-times_1322565650_banner.png)[0m                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### Key takeaways[0m                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Best-in-class companies with strong brands, deep competitive moats, and recurring revenues may be well positioned to adapt to a changing landscape and [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mnavigate future surprises.[0m                                                                                                                                   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* The old distinctions that used to separate "blue chip stocks" and "growth stocks" have blurred in the age of big tech.[0m                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Fidelity portfolio managers have found high-quality companies across consumer, communications, health care, tech, and other sectors.[0m                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m* Investors can "think like a fund manager" by potentially using future periods of volatility to buy quality stocks that they like at discounted prices.[0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mUncertainty is a perennial challenge in investing. In any market environment, investors may face a host of known unknowns, plus the unseen risks of unknown[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32munknowns.[0m                                                                                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m2026 is no different. While in many ways [the outlook appears strong](https://www.fidelity.com/learning-center/trading-investing/economic-outlook), there [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mare also profound forces of change and risk at work—from a frayed web of global trade, to the tense state of domestic and international affairs, to the [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlong-term challenges posed by high global indebtedness.[0m                                                                                                      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAmid heightened uncertainty, one way to manage risk is by leaning into high-quality companies—businesses with the strength to adapt and thrive as [0m           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mconditions change. Says Sonu Kalra, manager of **Fidelity® Blue Chip Growth Fund ([0m                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m [0m                                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFBGRX[0m                                                                                                                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m)**, “In the midst of extreme policy uncertainty, high-quality companies with deep competitive moats, pricing power, and strong brands may be best [0m          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpositioned to navigate the unknown.”[0m                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mNo one knows exactly which stocks will lead in the year ahead. But Fidelity portfolio managers have identified a number of companies that could thrive [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mthrough a variety of environments—blue-chip stocks in a range of industries, with the resilience to potentially prosper through volatility and to compound [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mearnings over time.[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m“Uncertainty is the new certainty,” says Sammy Simnegar, manager of **Fidelity® Magellan Fund ([0m                                                              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m [0m                                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mFMAGX[0m                                                                                                                                                        [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m)**. “Quality tends to work when there’s uncertainty.”[0m                                                                                                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### The charm of recurring revenues[0m                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mThere is no standard or single statistical definition of quality in investing, and fund managers tend to accentuate somewhat different characteristics. [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSimnegar looks for "the 3 Bs—brands, barriers to entry, and a best-in-class management team.” But, to him, the single best indicator of quality is the [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpredictability of earnings.[0m                                                                                                                                  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mTo measure this, Simnegar uses the volatility of earnings-per-share estimates—i.e., how much analysts’ projections about a given company’s profits tend to [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32magree or diverge. He notes that businesses with robust recurring revenues, such as those with subscription-based business models, often score well. “These [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcompanies generally offer a unique combination of predictability, growth, and resilience, making them what I consider to be cornerstones of stable, [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlong-term investing,” he says. “I think about subscription-based business models like a tollbooth, collecting a steady stream of revenue regardless of [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmarket conditions.”[0m                                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Costco Wholesale ([0m                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m [0m                                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mCOST[0m                                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m)**1 has been a good illustration of these dynamics at work, recently showing very low volatility of estimated future earnings, says Simnegar. This [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mpredictability, he says, stems from the fact that Costco makes about two-thirds of its profits from membership fees and operates its core warehouse [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mbusiness on such low margins that it crowds out competitors. “People pay to go to Costco because they count on great prices,” he says.[0m                       [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m**Verisk Analytics ([0m                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m [0m                                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mVRSK[0m                                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m)**2 is another “tollbooth” example in a completely different industry. Verisk provides analytics and risk-assessment software to the insurance industry [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mglobally. Simnegar says that more than 80% of its revenues in recent quarters have been generated by subscriptions, which provide a very high level of [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mrecurring cash flow. Again, a key indicator he has favored is that the volatility of estimated earnings has been very low—potentially implying a high level[0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mof predictability.[0m                                                                                                                                           [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIn a similar vein, Simnegar has been drawn to **Amazon ([0m                                                                                                     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m [0m                                                                                                                                                            [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mAMZN[0m                                                                                                                                                         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m)**,3 which he says earns “annuity-type” fees each year through its Amazon Prime and Prime Video subscription services, in addition to taking a cut of [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mretail sales on its e-commerce site. Of course, the company has also been benefitting from booming revenues in its Amazon Web Services division. “Amazon’s [0m  [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mmodel is like an online Costco, but also with a cloud business,” he says.[0m                                                                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m### Blue chips, yesterday and today[0m                                                                                                                          [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mOften overlooked is the shifting nature of “quality blue chips” versus “growth stocks” in today’s stock market. Before big tech reshaped the market [0m         [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mlandscape, typical blue chips were consumer staples companies, such as beverage or household-product businesses, that grew consistently but slowly, paid [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32msteady dividends, and might grow annual earnings per share by a point or 2 more than the average company. To find companies with high growth potential, [0m     [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32minvestors typically focused on small companies—seeking to identify up-and-comers that might ultimately blossom into mid- and large-cap market darlings.[0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mIt’s a different era now. “The fastest growers have been the winners in this market,” says Asher Anolic, co-manager of **Fidelity® Contrafund ([0m              [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mWe're sorry, quotes are currently unavailable. Please try again.[0m                                                                                             [32m│[0m
