[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mSherwood likes to look for quality on sale in sectors with dislocations that appear to be temporary. Two areas that have recently attracted his interest [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32minclude health care and applications software. Health care has underperformed the market significantly over the past 3 years due to policy headwinds and [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32muncertainty. Applications software stocks have been hammered by the perception that AI will undermine their business models, by enabling almost anyone to [0m   [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mcreate their own software. But both sectors offer “a lot of high-quality companies with strong business models,” he says.[0m                                    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m                                                                                                                                                               [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32m“The market has had a sell-first-and-ask-questions-later mindset with applications software,” Sherwood says. In his estimation, the fears are overblown, [0m    [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32mespecially for “vertical software” companies that concentrate in market niches and have been deeply embedded into their customers’ businesses for many [0m      [32m│[0m
[32m│[0m  [32myears, with mission-critical software. Two examples of this theme have been **Descartes Systems ([0m                                                            [32m│[0m
